<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abu Hamza al-Mukhtar ibn Awf</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 748</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abu Hamza al-Mukhtar ibn Awf was an Ibadi Kharijite leader and the general of Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn Yahya, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a> proclaimed in Hadramawt in 746. In 747 he marched north, defeated a Medinan army at Qudayd and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/medina">Medina</a>, where his sermons were long remembered. An Umayyad army under Ibn Atiyya defeated and killed him soon afterwards.</p></div>
